We apply classical post-processing to eliminate over-counting and identify unique vortex detections. Each circuit applied to each patch returns a binary value of $\mathcal{M}_{p,q}(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)$. The \ac{QVD} model therefore often detects the same vortex multiple times across neighboring contour evaluations. To count unique vortices only, we average regions where multiple detections occur, such that $\mathcal{M}_q(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)$ provides $0$ or $1$ detection values over the set of contour values. This post-processing can also aid in determining the central locations of the vortices.
