    \caption{\textbf{Trainability and generalizability of the \ac{QVD} model using Bayesian optimization.} Curves and dots represent the median, and shaded areas represent the inter-quartile range as obtained from $5$ instances with different seed values. \textbf{(a)} Training and testing of the model where we use optimization to minimize the \ac{MSE} with respect to the model's parameters. The loss history is shown for a model trained on $45$ fields and tested on $15$ fields. A final \ac{MSE} loss of $0.6$ for the train set and $0.7$ for the test set is reached after $20$ epochs. \textbf{(b)} The generalizability of the model where optimization is used to maximize the accuracy with respect to the model's parameters. Accuracy is optimized on a growing training set and evaluated on a separate test set of size $30$ containing only unseen fields.}    
