    \begin{abstract}
    We determine the precise number of isomorphism classes of elliptic curves over $\mathbb{F}_q(t)$ with $\text{char}(\mathbb{F}_q) = 3,2$. The key idea is to obtain the exact unweighted number of rational points on the classifying stacks $\mathcal{B} Q_{12}$, $\mathcal{B} Q_{24}$ and $\mathcal{B} Z$, where $Q_{12}$ and $Q_{24}$ denote the dicyclic groups of orders 12 and 24, respectively, and $Z$ denotes the non-reduced group scheme of order 2. This computation, inspired by the classical work of \cite{dJ2} and performed via motivic height zeta functions of height moduli spaces constructed in \cite{BPS}, establishes a complete determination of the total number of isomorphism classes of rational points on $\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}$ over any rational function field $k(t)$ with perfect residue field $\text{char}(k) \ge 0$.
    \end{abstract}

    %We combine the classical work of de Jong \cite{dJ2} with the height moduli framework of Bejleri–Park–Satriano \cite{BPS} to obtain an exact count of isomorphism classes of elliptic curves over rational function fields in all characteristics. In particular, we determine the precise number of isomorphism classes of elliptic curves over $K = \Fb_q(t)$ in characteristics $\text{char}(\Fb_q) = 2,3$. Together with the results of \cite{BPS}, which establish exact counts via motivic height zeta functions of height moduli spaces and their associated inertia stacks, this yields a complete determination of the unweighted count of rational points on $\Me$—that is, of isomorphism classes of elliptic curves $E/K$—over rational function fields $K = k(t)$ in all characteristics $\text{char}(k) \geq 0$.


