\subsection{Hyperparameter spaces}\label{SecA.1}


We use the Python package \texttt{hyperopt} from \url{https://hyperopt.github.io/hyperopt/} for tuning all predictive models. The tuning procedure is introduced as follows. The full dataset is split into three subsamples, representing the training and validation sets, which constitute 80\% and 20\% of the full dataset, respectively. To determine the optimal hyperparameters for our predictive models, we assess $R\in \{30, 100\}$ distinct sets. Utilizing the Python package \texttt{hyperopt}, we perform hyperparameter sampling in each round. The training set is used to train a model based on the sampled hyperparameters. Subsequently, the model's performance is evaluated on the validation set to score each set of hyperparameters. After conducting this process for $R$ rounds, we select the set with the highest evaluation scores as the best hyperparameters. A final predictive model is then trained using this optimal set, taking into account the full dataset. The hyperparameter spaces of boosted 01Neuro, Random Forests, XGBoost are respectively given in Table~\ref{tab:validation_sapce_01neuro} and Tables~\ref{tab:validation_sapce_rf}--\ref{tab:validation_sapce_xgb}.






