    %    Let \(A,B\) be metric open balls whose closure is contained in the interior of the annulus \(S^{n-1}\times [0,1]\), where the metric is inherited from embedding the annulus in \(\mathbb{R}^n\). There exists a homeomorphism of the annulus \(h\) such that \(h(A)\subseteq B\) and \(h\restriction S^n\times \{0,1\}=id\).
