  \begin{proposition}[\csct{} semantics with Dirac initial configuration]\label{prop:CSCTDiracInit}
    Assuming the setting of \cref{def:ConfMCCSCT}, if the configuration $d$ is a Dirac distribution, then the transition function $\delta_{\mathbb{X}^{\csct{}},\sigma}$ acting on $d$ is a distribution over Dirac distribution. That is, concretely, for any Dirac distributions $d,d'\in\dist(Q)$ with supports $q,q'\in Q$ respectively, the transition function yields a distribution over Dirac distribution as follows,
    $$\delta_{\mathbb{X}^{\csct{}},\sigma}(d)(d')=\sum_{a\in\act}\sigma(d)(a)\cdot\delta(q,a)(q').$$

