Hence inductively, the set of all initial configurations that are reachable to $H$ is also upward-closed, which motivates the usage of antichains since they are a canonical representation of upward-closed sets. Formally, we connect this observation to \cref{prob:csmt-reach-deter} with the following theorem, which characterizes the set of configurations reaching $H$ as the least fixed point of an operator that preserves upward-closeness.

