\begin{abstract}

  % We introduce Mesh Silksong, a compact and efficient mesh representation tailored for auto-regressive models, enabling the generation of artistic meshes in a manner akin to silk weaving. 
  % Unlike existing mesh-token compression methods, our approach compresses each mesh vertex only once, reducing the redundancy of the token sequence by 50\% and achieving a state-of-the-art compression rate of approximately 22\%. Beyond generating highly detailed artistic meshes, our method produces meshes with superior geometric properties that are absent in current methods, including manifold topology, watertight detection, and consistent face normals, which are critical for practical applications. 
