\begin{abstract}
In this study, we introduce the generalized Schwartz space  $\mathcal{S}_{k,n}(\R)$, designed specifically for the  $\left(k,\frac{2}{n}\right)-$generalized Fourier transform $\mathcal{F}_{k,n}:=\mathcal{F}_{k,\frac{2}{n}}$. We establish that \(\mathcal{S}_{k,n}(\mathbb{R})\) is invariant under \(\mathcal{F}_{k,n}\) and explore its principal properties in detail. Furthermore, by defining the subspace $\mathcal{D}_{k,n}(\R)$, consisting of functions with bounded support, we show that the subspace is dense in $L^p(d\mu_{k,n})$ for $1 \leq p < \infty$. Lastly, we address a conjecture regarding the higher-dimensional scenario.
\end{abstract}

