The main purpose of the  labels for us is that they will enable us to `import' certain technical results concerning the full transformation monoid $\T_n$ from \cite{GR12}.
Throughout we will identify~$\T_n$ with its natural copy inside $\P_n$, i.e.~with the set of all partitions
with full domain and trivial cokernel; see Subsection \ref{ss:Pn}. 
In \cite[Subsection 2.5]{GR12} a labelling function was defined for idempotents in $\T_n$, and it is easy to check that this is the restriction to $E(\T_n)$ of our labelling of~$E(\P_n)$.
The following facts are also clear.


\newpage

\begin{lemma}
\label{la:lamprops}
