We can now complete the proof of the proposition.
We have seen that we can eliminate all the generators, except for a single $a_t$, for $t\in P_2$.
Thus $\GI \cong \sfG(T)$ is cyclic. But $\GI$ is infinite by Proposition \ref{prop:preimage}, so it follows that indeed $\GI\cong\Z$.
\end{proof}
