 \item $x_{11}$: Distance to the town hall (distance by the roads) 
 \item $x_{15}$: Aggregate: Year built \& Number of storeys 
\end{description}

As binary  features we used the factors describing the storey of the flat (“the first”, “the last”); the wall material of the building (“bricky”, “large-panel”, “monolithic”, “small-element concrete blocks”; at the same time the wall materials such as “made of timber” and “not determined” were excluded from consideration because they are nonrepresentational and don’t have economic substance). Thus we used 17  features for modeling. We created all kinds of combinations of these factors using RuleFit (we create models with the number of factors from 8 to 12). We created 86632 ($\sum_{k=8}^{12}C_{17}^k$) models in total.  For a selection of the best model we used values of $R^2$ and $MAE$; and also we checked the signs of variables according to their economic substance. In order to keep the interpretability of the model we applied a limit on the number of rules as a hyperparameter of the model – 50 rules. For a generation of rules we used the Random Forest algorithm. As a result of LASSO the part of rules were evaluated as insignificant and excluded, and only significant were kept. The final model contains 22 rules and 12  features. They are shown in the Table ~\ref{tab:tab5}. Due to its volume, we present it in the ~\ref{rf_res}.

